      "authorType": "TOPIC",
      "competitionRanking": 1971,
      "content": "<p>I submitted the same <code>submission.zip</code> multiple times, and got different scores.<br>\nAs per comments in other threads, many other participants can also observe this.</p>\n<p>This is only possible if the <code>temperature</code> parameter during evaluation is something other than <code>0</code>. In the evaluation section of the competition overview, it's written that <code>temparature</code> is supposed to be <code>0</code>. Perhaps, there's a mistake in the evaluation code? It's possible because the default value of <code>temparature</code> is set to <code>1.0</code> in the evaluation metric notebook.  </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/ryanholbrook\" target=\"_blank\">@ryanholbrook</a> can you please look into this? Can you please make sure that the evaluation code is correctly overriding the function's default temperature parameter?</p>",
      "feedbackTrackingData": {},
      "id": 3430976,
      "isThankYou": false,
      "kernelVersion": 0,
      "parent": {},
      "postDate": "2026-03-29T06:49:15.217Z",
      "rawMarkdown": "I submitted the same `submission.zip` multiple times, and got different scores.  \nAs per comments in other threads, many other participants can also observe this.\n\nThis is only possible if the `temperature` parameter during evaluation is something other than `0`. In the evaluation section of the competition overview, it's written that `temparature` is supposed to be `0`. Perhaps, there's a mistake in the evaluation code? It's possible because the default value of `temparature` is set to `1.0` in the evaluation metric notebook.  \n\n@ryanholbrook can you please look into this? Can you please make sure that the evaluation code is correctly overriding the function's default temperature parameter?",
